        <description> 
            The Docking Camera (DCAM) is a custom-built CMOS monochrome camera from Malin Space Science Systems. 
            It was in-cabin mounted to capture imagery out the docking window of the Artemis II Orion spacecraft 
            during the mission. The camera primarily supported the Proximity Operations (Prox Ops) demonstration 
            about 3 hours into the mission. During Prox Ops, the DCAM was used to visualize the detached upper 
            stage of the SLS (Space Launch System) as the crew piloted Orion to simulate docking with a future 
            lunar lander. The DCAM collected additional imaging of both the Earth and Moon when they were in 
            their view or in support of other mission or Developmental Flight Test Objectives (DFTOs).
        </description>
    </Instrument>
